x_pool_size.\r\nif i just ignore the exception, everything works fine, but i think this should never happend.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\ni expect no exception thrown\r\n### Actual behavior\r\nthrow  java.lang.IllegalStateException: Channel is unhealthy not offering it back to pool.\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n1. Create FixedChannelPool.\r\n2. call aquire channel\r\n3. kill channel\r\n4. call release channel, but the returned ChannelFuture call get()\r\n5. TA DA throw  java.lang.IllegalStateException: Channel is unhealthy not offering it back to pool.\r\n\r\n### Minimal yet complete reproducer code (or URL to code)\r\n`public class MaybeBug {`\r\n`    @Test`\r\n`    public void test() throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException{`\r\n`        Bootstrap config = new Bootstrap();`\r\n`        config.remoteAddress(\"localhost\", 1234);`\r\n`        config.option(ChannelOption.TCP_NODELAY, true);`\r\n`        config.channel(NioSocketChannel.class);`\r\n`        config.group(new NioEventLoopGroup(1));`\r\n`        FixedChannelPool pool = new FixedChannelPool(config, new AbstractChannelPoolHandler() {`\r\n`            @Override`\r\n`            public void channelCreated(Channel ch) throws Exception {`\r\n`                /**`\r\n`                 * ignore`\r\n`                 */`\r\n`            }`\r\n`        }, 2);`\r\n`        Channel fresh = pool.acquire().get();`\r\n`        fresh.close().get();`\r\n`        pool.release(fresh).get();`\r\n`    }\r\n}`\r\n### Netty version\r\n4.1.5\r\n### JVM version (e.g. `java -version`)\r\n1.8\r\n### OS version (e.g. `uname -a`)\r\nWindows 10\r\n\r\nNB: sorry for bad english.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/followers","following_url":"h